[AC-034:288](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:288).

   **SPEC fix:** Define first-use admission so expired keys remain rejectable after record cleanup—for example, 
server-verifiable key freshness or durable content-free tombstones. Extend AC-034 to replay an expired key **after 
actual retention cleanup**, asserting no provider dispatch through real routes and Supabase.

2. **R4-2 — Low — AC-032: the mixed insertion fixture masks the concurrency defect.**

   **Problem/scenario:** At 99 items, Apply of two items already exceeds capacity independently of the competing 
manual addition. That test can pass even if Apply does not share atomic capacity enforcement with manual insertion. 
The reachable defect is at 98 items, where a manual addition and a two-item Apply each fit independently but together 
produce 101.

   **Evidence:** [FR-011:112](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:112), 
[AC-032:286](E:/projects/virtual-office/spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/SPEC.md:286).

   **SPEC fix:** Race manual addition against a **one-item Apply at 99 items**, or a **two-item Apply at 98**. 
