every viewer of the note. | r1 q13, r2 q12, r4. |
148: | BR-011 | A change based on an outdated note revision is rejected. | r1 q18. |
149: | BR-012 | AI access uses API keys only; no subscription credentials are requested, stored, or proxied. | 
Anthropic policy; r3. |
150: | BR-013 | A processing uses the settings snapshot taken at admission; settings changes affect only later 
admissions; no silent fallback between providers. | Privacy notice fidelity; review H4. |
151: 
152: ## 9. Data and integrations
153: 
154: ### Data inputs
155: 
156: - Note fields, participants, rich-text content, action items, transcript files (.txt/.vtt/.srt, UTF-8 text, ≤1 
MB).
157: - Admin AI settings: provider, API key, model, reasoning level, daily limit.
158: 
159: ### Data outputs
160: 
161: - Stored notes, versions, participants, action items, transcripts, AI settings metadata, encrypted keys, usage 
records.
162: - AI drafts (transient until applied).
163: - Search results with excerpts; downloaded .md files.
164: 
165: ### Integrations
166: 
167: - Anthropic Messages API (official SDK), OpenAI API (official SDK), Kimi (Moonshot) and GLM (Zhipu/Z.ai) through 
their OpenAI-compatible endpoints; each adapter sends only parameters valid for its provider and model (curated 
capability matrix). All calls are server-side from authenticated API routes.
168: - Supabase Postgres (RLS, full-text search), Supabase Auth.
169: 
170: ### Database contracts (migrations required; local first)
171: 
172: - `meeting_notes`: add immutable `company_id`; author as historical id + name snapshots plus a live `created_by` 
reference (ON DELETE SET NULL); a revision column, content storage, and search vector; make `summary` optional; make 
`room_id` nullable with ON DELETE SET NULL; `company_id` → companies ON DELETE CASCADE.
173: - New structures: note versions (historical fields immutable; editor historical id + name snapshot; live editor 
reference ON DELETE SET NULL is the only permitted change), note participants (with name snapshot), AI settings 
(metadata, revision), encrypted key storage (no client grants), daily usage reservations/records and operation records 
with idempotency keys (no content; 30-day retention).
174: - `meeting_note_action_items`: date-only due date (`date`), assignee name snapshot, per-item revision, 
completion-only path for assignees.
175: - RLS and grants for every table, with writes through authorized routes/RPCs; indexes for search 
(accent-insensitive Portuguese/English) and for list ordering.
176: - Legacy rows: before applying online, a read-only preflight on `vhabpcoyypobgasacsko` counts existing 
`meeting_notes`/items; if any exist, the owner decides their company/author backfill before the migration is applied.
177: - Rollback: application first; database rollback must not restore the cascade that deletes notes with their space.
178: - The existing `IMeetingNoteRepository`, `SupabaseMeetingNoteRepository`, and `MeetingNote`/`ActionItem` types 
are reused and extended (no runtime caller exists today).
179: 
180: ## 10. Constraints and assumptions
181: 
182: ### Constraints
183: 
184: - Next.js App Router, TypeScript strict, Supabase Postgres/Auth/RLS, TanStack Query, shadcn/ui, following 
AGENTS.md (server client in routes, `auth.getUser()`, `users.id` vs `users.supabase_uid`, roles `admin|member`).
185: - API keys and transcript text never appear in client code, logs, error messages, analytics, or reports; provider 
errors are mapped to sanitized messages.
186: - AI calls only from the server; the browser never calls a provider.
187: - Size limits: title ≤200 chars; content ≤100,000 chars; ≤50 participants; ≤100 action items per note; item 
description ≤1,000 chars; transcript ≤1 MB.
188: - UI in the app's current language (English); AI summary in the transcript's language.
189: - Migrations are written and applied locally during the phase; applied to the online database 
`vhabpcoyypobgasacsko` only at phase end with the owner's explicit authorization, after the read-only preflight, 
followed by catalog readback and a runtime smoke check. Rollout: migrations, then app.
190: - Only integration and E2E tests (no unit tests); one test process at a time; one final Chrome-only E2E run.
191: 
192: ### Assumptions
193: 
194: - The owner creates an OpenAI platform API key (billed separately from ChatGPT Plus/Pro) for the final test 
against the real provider (confirmed r3).
195: - Automated tests use a local fake AI server compatible with the provider APIs (confirmed r2 q17).
196: 
197: ## 11. Edge cases and failure modes
198: 
199: | Case | Expected behavior |
200: |---|---|
201: | Two editors change the same note concurrently (edit, restore, attach, Apply) | The later change is rejected 
with a conflict warning showing the newer state (FR-007). |
202: | Editor edits an item while the assignee toggles completion | Each succeeds only against the item's current 
revision; the stale one gets a conflict. |
203: | Empty / >1 MB / wrong extension / binary file | Rejected before any change or AI call; not counted (FR-013). |
204: | .vtt/.srt with cue numbers and timestamps | Stripped; speaker names kept (FR-014). |
205: | Transcript too large for the configured model | Refused before dispatch with guidance; not counted (FR-020). |
206: | Provider error, timeout, refusal, malformed/truncated output | Note and transcript unchanged; error + "Try 
again"; counted if dispatched and processed (FR-021, FR-022). |
207: | Invalid key or provider unavailable before processing | Error + "Try again"; not counted (FR-022). |
208: | User leaves the page while processing | Draft discarded; counted if already dispatched (FR-022). |
209: | Several members start processing at 19/20 | At most one is admitted; the others are refused by the limit 
(FR-022). |
210: | Network retry of the start request | Same idempotency key and binding → same result, no second dispatch or 
count; changed binding → rejected (FR-031). |
211: | Server crash between dispatch and recording | Reservation stays counted (FR-022). |
212: | Provider accepts the request but the connection drops before the response | No automatic retry; counted; user 
sees error + "Try again" (new admission) (FR-016, FR-022). |
213: | Member is removed from the company while their processing runs | Draft discarded at return; Apply rechecks 
rights (FR-018, FR-021). |
214: | Another editor replaces the transcript or edits the note while a draft is pending | Apply refused as a conflict 
against the draft's source revision (FR-018). |
215: | Author or version editor's user row is deleted | Notes and history kept with id and name snapshots (FR-029). |
216: | Two items added at 99 items, or an add racing with Apply | At most one succeeds; total never exceeds 100; a 
refused Apply changes nothing (FR-011). |
217: | Member signs out or is removed while a response is in flight | Browser drops the late response; drafts and 
cached notes cleared (FR-021). |
218: | Browser replays a start request days later | Ticket expired → rejected; never dispatched, even after record 
cleanup (FR-031). |
219: | Server crashes mid-processing | Operation becomes "failed" after 10 minutes, stays counted; Try again uses a 
new key (FR-031). |
220: | Admin changes provider/key/model after a member saw the notice | Start refused, new notice shown; 
already-admitted processings finish on their snapshot (FR-015, BR-013). |
221: | AI suggests a name matching no member or several members | Item unassigned (FR-017). |
222: | Suggestion duplicates an existing item | Unchecked, "already exists" (FR-018). |
223: | Apply would exceed 100 items | Refused with message (FR-018). |
224: | Daily limit reached | Refused with limit and reset time (FR-023). |
225: | No AI configured | Manual notes work; AI disabled with message; admin sees settings link (FR-025). |
226: | Space deleted | Notes kept, "Space removed" (FR-028). |
227: | Company deleted | Its notes are deleted (FR-028). |
228: | Participant/assignee leaves, is deleted, or rejoins | "Former member", no access; rights return on rejoin 
(FR-030). |
229: | Viewer tries to add themselves as participant (UI or direct DB) | Denied (BR-003, BR-004). |
230: | Assignee tries to change description, assignee, or note of an item | Denied (BR-005). |
231: | Transcript contains instructions aimed at the AI | Treated as data; output validated against a fixed schema; 
extra fields dropped; assignees resolved only against current members. |
232: | AI output contains HTML/script or Markdown injection | Sanitized in view, escaped in export. |
233: | Member of company A requests anything of company B (note, version, item, search, settings, usage) | Nothing 
returned / denied (SM-3). |
234: | Non-admin calls the AI settings route | Denied (BR-009). |
235: 
236: ## 12. Security, privacy, compliance, and abuse considerations
237: 
238: - RLS on every new or changed table, comparing `users.supabase_uid` with `auth.uid()::text` and scoping by the 
note's stored `company_id`; API routes resolve the application user by `supabase_uid`; authorization uses the 
pre-change state.
239: - Column-level protection: completion-only path for assignees; immutable `company_id`, `created_by`, `note_id`, 
creation times; versions are insert-only.
240: - API keys encrypted at rest in server-only storage (no authenticated/anon grants, no Realtime publication), 
decrypted only inside server code for a dispatch, never returned, never logged; provider error bodies sanitized.
241: - Rich text sanitized on write and render; AI output treated as untrusted; Markdown export escapes HTML.
242: - Only transcript text goes to a third-party provider (never the member roster), and only after the notice naming 
that provider for the current settings revision; the admin's provider choice (including providers hosted outside 
Brazil/US) is the company's decision.
243: - Abuse and cost: daily limit counted at dispatch with atomic reservations and idempotency; size and context 
preflight; server-side validation of every limit.
244: - Subscription credentials (Claude, ChatGPT) are never requested or stored.
245: 
246: ## 13. Accessibility, localization, and usability considerations
247: 
248: - Editor, version list, review step, and dialogs are keyboard-operable with visible focus and labelled controls 
(Radix/shadcn primitives).
249: - Clear progress state while processing; errors state what happened and what to do.
250: - UI strings in English, matching the app; summary language follows the transcript; dates shown in the user's 
local time; the reset time shown in the user's local time.
251: - Interactive elements inside clickable cards follow the AGENTS.md interaction rules.
252: 
253: ## 14. Acceptance criteria
254: 
255: - AC-001 (FR-001, FR-003, FR-005, BR-002): Given a member of company A, when they create a note in a private 
space with title, today's date, two participants, and content using bold, a heading, a list, a checklist, and a link, 
then it is listed first in that space's Notes tab and opens showing all fields with the formatting rendered; when they 
create a second note dated last month, then it is listed after the first.
256: - AC-002 (FR-001, FR-011, BR-001): Given an empty title, a missing date, a 201-char title, content above 100,000 
chars, 51 participants, or a participant who is not a current member of company A, when saving, then the save is 
rejected with a message and nothing is stored.
257: - AC-003 (FR-002, FR-027): Given content and AI output containing a script tag, an `onerror` attribute, and a 
`javascript:` link, when saved, viewed, and exported, then no script runs, the unsafe link is neutralized, and the 
export contains no raw HTML from user text.
258: - AC-004 (FR-006, BR-003, BR-004): Given a note by X with participant Y, when Y and an admin of company A edit 
it, then both succeed; when non-participant Z edits, adds themselves as participant, or restores a version — through 
the UI, the API route, and a direct Supabase client call — then each is denied and Z sees no edit control; when an 
admin of company B attempts the same, then it is denied.
259: - AC-005 (FR-007, BR-011): Given two sessions loaded the same revision, when each saves different content (and 
separately: one restores while the other saves; one attaches a transcript while the other applies a draft), then the 
first succeeds, the second gets a conflict warning showing the newer state, and the first's change is intact.
260: - AC-006 (FR-008, FR-009, BR-007): Given a note saved three times, when a viewer opens history, then three 
versions show who and when and cannot be modified by any role; when a non-editor viewer tries to restore, then it is 
denied; when an editor restores version 1, then a fourth version equals version 1's fields (including participants) 
and action items and the transcript are unchanged.
261: - AC-007 (FR-010, BR-003): Given a note with versions, items, participants, and a transcript, when the author 
confirms delete, then all of them are gone; when a participant who is neither author nor admin tries to delete, then 
it is denied.
262: - AC-008 (FR-011, BR-005): Given a note editor, when they add, edit, and delete an item with description, 
assignee, and due date, then each change is shown; when the assignee (not an editor) toggles completion, then it 
succeeds; when the assignee changes the description, assignee, due date, or note of the item, or toggles another 
person's item, then it is denied.
263: - AC-009 (FR-011): Given a note with 10 items, when adding an item with an empty or 1,001-char description, or 
with an assignee who left the company or belongs to another company, then each is rejected; given a note with 100 
items, when adding a valid 101st, then it is rejected for capacity; a due date saved as 2026-11-05 is displayed as 
2026-11-05 in every timezone.
264: - AC-010 (FR-012, FR-015, FR-016, FR-018, BR-006, BR-010): Given a configured provider (fake AI server in 
automated tests), when a member uploads a valid .txt via "New note from transcript", then the note exists immediately 
with title = file name, today's date, and the transcript; a notice names the provider; processing returns a draft that 
changes nothing until Apply; after editing the summary, reassigning one suggestion, rejecting one, and accepting 
another, Apply stores exactly the edited summary and the two accepted items and creates one version; when an editor 
attaches a new transcript to a note, then the stored transcript is replaced immediately and the summary is unchanged.
265: - AC-011 (FR-013): Given an empty file, a 1.1 MB file, a .pdf renamed .txt, a .docx, and a Latin-1 binary blob, 
when uploading, then each is rejected with a message, no note is created or changed, no AI call is made, and usage is 
unchanged.
266: - AC-012 (FR-014): Given a .vtt and a .srt with cue numbers, timestamps, cue settings, and speaker names, when 
processed, then the text received by the fake provider contains no cue numbers, timestamps, or cue settings and keeps 
speaker names and spoken text.
267: - AC-013 (FR-016, FR-017, BR-006): Given a draft suggesting "Ana" when exactly one current member is named Ana, 
"Bruno" when two members match, "Carla" when none does, and "Diego" who left the company, then only Ana is pre-linked 
and the others are unassigned; the request received by the fake provider contains the transcript and no member names 
that are absent from the transcript.
268: - AC-014 (FR-004, FR-026, BR-001, SM-2, SM-3): Given 1,000 notes in company A and notes in company B with the 
same words, when a member of A searches a word that appears only in a title, only in content, only in a summary, and 
only in an action-item description, in Portuguese with and without accents and in English with different case, with 
and without space and period filters, then each returns the matching notes of A within the filters, ordered by 
relevance then meeting date, paginated, with excerpts; the first page returns within 1 second locally; no note of B 
appears.
269: - AC-015 (FR-004): Given the dashboard, when the member clicks "AI Meeting Notes", then the Meetings page opens.
270: - AC-016 (FR-021, FR-022, FR-023, BR-008): Given the fake provider returns an error after processing, times out, 
refuses, or returns malformed JSON, then the note and transcript are unchanged, an error with "Try again" appears, and 
usage increases by one each; given it rejects the key or is unavailable before processing, then usage is unchanged; 
given the user navigates away after dispatch, then no draft is applied and usage increases by one; given a successful 
draft that the user never applies, then usage increases by one; given the company reached its limit, then processing 
is refused with the limit and reset time; at 00:00 America/Sao_Paulo the count resets.
271: - AC-017 (FR-024, BR-009): Given an admin, when they save provider, key, model, reasoning level, and limit 50, 
then the settings persist and the key is shown only as its last four characters; a canary key string never appears in 
any API response, company read, direct Supabase select (any role), Realtime payload, server log line, or client 
bundle; when a member calls the settings route, then it is denied; limit 0 or 201 is rejected; a company that never 
saved settings has limit 20.
272: - AC-018 (FR-025): Given no provider configured, when a member opens a note, then manual editing works and AI 
controls are disabled with "An admin needs to configure AI"; an admin additionally sees a link to settings.
273: - AC-019 (FR-005, FR-027): Given a note with formatted content, summary, items, and transcript, when exported 
without the option, then the .md contains title, date, space, author, participants, Markdown content, summary, and 
items but no transcript; with the option ticked, the transcript is included.
274: - AC-020 (FR-028, FR-029): Given a space with notes, when the space is deleted, then its notes remain on the 
Meetings page and in search labelled "Space removed", keep their author and company, and remain editable by the same 
people; when a company is deleted, then its notes are deleted.
275: - AC-021 (FR-030): Given a participant and assignee who leaves the company, then the note shows "Former member" 
with the snapshot name and that user can no longer read the note; when the user row is deleted, then the snapshot name 
still shows; when they rejoin the same company, then their participant rights return; saving the note while a former 
member is still listed succeeds.
276: - AC-022 (SM-1, BR-012): Given the owner's OpenAI API key configured on the new app against the online database, 
when processing the one-hour fixture transcript, then the draft appears within 60 seconds; at no point is a 
subscription login requested.
277: - AC-023 (SM-3, BR-001, BR-009, FR-029): Given two companies, when a member and an admin of each attempt direct 
API and database access to the other's notes, versions, participants, items, transcripts, search, AI settings, keys, 
and usage, then every attempt returns nothing or is denied, and `company_id`/`created_by` cannot be changed by any 
client.
278: - AC-024 (FR-012): Given an existing note, when a non-editor tries to attach a transcript, then it is denied and 
the stored transcript is unchanged.
279: - AC-025 (FR-015, BR-013): Given a member saw the notice for provider P at settings revision R, when the admin 
switches to provider Q before the member starts, then the start is refused and the notice for Q is shown; a processing 
already admitted under P completes on P.
280: - AC-026 (FR-016, FR-020, FR-024): Given each of the four provider adapters configured against the fake server, 
when processing, then each sends only its valid parameters for the selected model and reasoning level and returns a 
draft; given a transcript whose estimated size exceeds the configured model's budget, then it is refused before 
dispatch and usage is unchanged.
281: - AC-027 (FR-018, FR-019): Given a note with three items (one completed) and a stored transcript, when an editor 
reprocesses and the draft repeats one existing item and proposes two new ones, then the repeated one arrives unchecked 
as "already exists", Apply appends only the accepted new items, and the three existing items (including completion) 
are unchanged; when Apply would exceed 100 items, then it is refused.
282: - AC-028 (FR-022, FR-031): Given the company is at 19 of 20, when five processing requests start concurrently, 
then exactly one is dispatched and counted and four are refused; when a start request is replayed with the same key 
and binding (including after midnight America/Sao_Paulo), then the fake provider receives it once and usage counts it 
once; when the same key is sent for a different note or transcript, then it is rejected; when a member calls any usage 
table or RPC directly to refund or alter usage, then it is denied.
283: - AC-029 (FR-016, FR-022): Given the fake provider accepts a request and the connection drops before its 
response, then the fake provider records exactly one received request, usage increases by one, and the user sees an 
error with "Try again"; for each adapter, given the fake provider returns as its initial response one of that 
adapter's listed rejection status/type/code combinations with its normal error body, then usage is unchanged; given an 
unlisted status or code, or an overload error after streaming has begun, then usage stays counted.
284: - AC-030 (FR-018, FR-021): Given the fake provider is paused mid-processing, when another editor replaces the 
transcript, then Apply of the returned draft is refused as a conflict; when instead an admin removes the requesting 
member from the company, then no draft is returned to them and nothing is applied.
285: - AC-031 (FR-029): Given a note authored by X and edited by Y, when X's and Y's user rows are deleted, then the 
deletion succeeds, the note and all versions remain, author and editor show their snapshot names, and their historical 
id snapshots are unchanged; no client role can modify historical fields.
286: - AC-032 (FR-011, FR-018): Given a note with 99 items, when two editors add an item concurrently, then exactly 
one succeeds; given a note with 98 items where a manual add and a two-item Apply each succeed alone, when they run 
concurrently, then the total never exceeds 100 and a refused Apply changes nothing.
287: - AC-033 (FR-021, SM-3): Given a processing whose route response is delayed, when the member signs out and 
another account signs in (and separately when the member is removed from the company) before the response arrives, 
then the late response is dropped and no draft or note of the previous scope appears.
288: - AC-034 (FR-021, FR-031): Given an operation cancelled by leaving the page that later completes, when its key is 
replayed, then the status is "discarded" with no draft and no new dispatch; given a ticket issued more than 24 hours 
ago, then the request is rejected as expired without dispatch, including after its operation records have been 
deleted; given the server process is killed after dispatch, then 10 minutes later the operation is "failed", usage 
stays counted, and deleting the note does not change usage.
289: 
290: ## 15. Test strategy
291: 
292: - Levels: integration and E2E only (AGENTS.md). No unit tests; no mocking of Supabase, repositories, or the code 
under test.
293: - Integration (Vitest against local Supabase and real API routes): RLS and route authorization per role and 
company, including direct-client attacks (AC-004, AC-006, AC-007, AC-008, AC-017, AC-021, AC-023, AC-024); validation 
limits (AC-002, AC-009, AC-011); revisions and conflicts with competing transactions (AC-005); versions (AC-006); 
transcript normalization (AC-012); assignee matching (AC-013); usage counting, reservations, idempotency, reset 
(AC-016, AC-028); settings revision binding (AC-025); outbound retries, refund classification, idempotency binding, 
replay, expiry and crash recovery, in-flight membership removal, draft source revision, user deletion, concurrent item 
capacity (AC-028–AC-032, AC-034); adapters and preflight (AC-026); reprocess merge (AC-027); search fields, languages, 
ordering, pagination, isolation, and timing with 1,000 seeded notes (AC-014); space and company deletion (AC-020); key 
canary (AC-017).
294: - External AI provider: replaced in automated tests only, by a local fake server speaking each provider's API, 
selected by environment configuration, recording received requests, with fixed responses and scripted failures (error 
after processing, timeout, refusal, malformed JSON, auth rejection, unavailable). Database, RLS, routes, and UI stay 
real.
295: - E2E (Playwright, two accounts): manual note lifecycle, rendering and sanitization, editing rights, conflict, 
history/restore, action items with assignee completion, transcript upload → review → Apply, reprocess, AI-disabled 
state, admin settings, search, export download, dashboard link, late responses across sign-out (AC-001, AC-003–AC-008, 
AC-010, AC-015, AC-018, AC-019, AC-027, AC-033).
296: - Test data: fictional transcripts in .txt/.vtt/.srt, Portuguese and English, including speaker names, accents, a 
one-hour fixture, and malformed files. No real personal data.
297: - Cadence: per task type-check + lint; per block type-check, lint, DB integration suite when server code changed; 
one final Chrome-only E2E run of all new specs plus the full regression suite, zero retries; one test process at a 
time.
298: - Owner test: AC-022 with a real OpenAI key against the online database after the migrations are applied.
299: 
300: ## 16. Validation and launch checklist
301: 
302: - All Must FRs and AC-001..AC-034 have evidence in TRACK.
303: - Adversarial reviews passed at SPEC, PLAN, each block, and final.
304: - Type-check, lint, build, DB integration suite, final E2E run green.
305: - Migrations listed with state: written locally, applied locally, preflight on `vhabpcoyypobgasacsko`, applied 
there after authorization, catalog read back, smoke check, app deployed.
306: - ROADMAP updated: Phase 6 status; MEET-08 moved to Phase 7.
